Hi everyone

I'm trying to plot data from fisheries models, specifically
overlapping observed (geom_bar) and fitted proportion (geom_line) of
fish versus its length (see botton post).  Follow the next code:

# catch at length plot
p <- ggplot(subset(reclas))
p1 <- p + geom_bar(aes(factor(length), obs), stat = "identity")
p2 <- p1 + facet_wrap(~year)
p3 <- p2 + geom_line(aes(factor(length), pre, group = 1))
p4 <- p3 + opts(axis.text.x = theme_text(hjust = 0))
p4

I get an expected plots, but the xlabel look very ugly!!!
Does anyone know how I can fit the xtick?

Ps: any recommendation about aesthetics is welcome!!! :-)

Thank a lot and Happy new year

