With some minor coding changes :

Datum<-c("2010-10-26","2010-10-26","2011-10-20","2011-10-20")
Provpunkt<-c("Sjö","Utlopp","Sjö","Utlopp")
Ptot<-c(0.01,0.011,0.01,0.01)
Prange<-c(NA,NA,0.01,0.01)
Hav<-cbind(Datum,Provpunkt, Ptot, Prange)

Hav <- as.data.frame(Hav) # <- line added

theme_set(theme_bw())
opts <- opts(
  plot.title = theme_text(size=36),
  axis.text.x = theme_text(size=24,angle=90),
  axis.text.y = theme_text(size=24),
  axis.title.y = theme_text(size=28,angle=90),
  legend.text = theme_text(size=24),
  legend.title = theme_text(size=28,hjust=0),
  title="P-tot"
)

ggplot(aes(x = Datum, y = Ptot, colour = Provpunkt), data = Hav) +
  geom_point(size=10) + geom_path(size=2) + labs(x = "", y = "mg/l") +
  geom_linerange(aes(x=Datum, ymin=0,ymax=Prange)) + opts

Runs fine (but looks pretty bad).  I think you had a few main issues : 1. hav was capitalized in one instance, and not in the other, 2. it was not a data.frame, and 3. you had the +'s after the line breaks, when they needed to be before.

Hope it helps, now you can just go straight away with ggsave.

Cheers
david.

