Yes, but ?stat::p.adjust doesn't tell you anything about what p-values
are and how to use them, or how to get them out of other tests, which
I feel like is what you want.

I totally agree that the ggplot2 documentation could be better, but
I'm not sure the right way to do that.  I don't think adding a lot of
duplication by explaining the same thing in multiple places would be a
big help.

> The first reference for ggplot newcomers is the documentation
