quite figure it out. Any help would be appreciated.

Here is an example data set.

stage<-c(rep(c("s","sm","m","l"),3))
stageNum<-c(rep(c(1:4),3))
mean<-
c(0,0.01250000,0.05590062,0.02857143,3.98437500,8.48603352,6.51162791,20.28571429,1.13793103,2.81395349,9.77192982,20.27450980)
se<-
c(0.00000000,0.01250000,0.02372272,0.02857143,0.78729331,1.44849337,1.23167767,12.04893650,0.79982162,0.72676252,1.27076721,4.32594348)
tsb<-c(rep(15,4),rep(16,4),rep(17,4))
tsbf<-as.factor(e)
tmp<-data.frame(a,aa,b,d,ef,e)

plot.1<-ggplot(tmp,aes(stageNum,mean,pch=tsbf))+geom_point(size=3,) +
geom_linerange(aes(ymax=mean+se,ymin=mean-se),size=1,position="dodge")
+ geom_line()

plot.2<-ggplot(tmp,aes(stageNum,mean,pch=tsb))+geom_point(size=3,) +
geom_linerange(aes(ymax=mean+se,ymin=mean-se),size=1,position="dodge")
+ geom_line()

## End ##

I want to graph the mean on the y axis and the stage on the x axis,
and draw lines connecting the stages for different tsb values.  In the
above data frame tsb is considered as a factor in plot.1 and numeric
in plot.2

Undesirable effects happen in both graphs. In plot.1, with tsb as a
factor everything looks fine, but the plot symbol numbers (15,16,17)
do not exactly correspond to numbers as usually used in R. (see
http://rgraphics.limnology.wisc.edu/pch.php).

However, if I change tsb to numeric, lines are not plotted correctly
along x axis.

Any suggestions? Also, how can I label the x axis with the values from
stage?

This seems like it should be simple, I just can't figure it out.

Thanks for any info

Wade

